{
  "$schema": "delivery-manifest-v1",
  "description": "Single source of truth for quay release artifacts. release.yml must produce exactly this set — no more, no less. The npm-pack (.tgz) and Node-SEA (single-file executable) lines were CANCELLED by the human ruling of 2026-09-16 (orchestration/SPEC-release-and-hotfix-branching-2026-09-15.md §11: 「取消 sea 和 npm release。这些是我们最近没有精力去保障的。」), so no npm-tarballs / sea-binaries entries are declared: release.yml no longer produces them, and a manifest that still declared them would be the drift this checker exists to catch. The release channel is the Claude Code plugin channel, gated by a real marketplace install of the released tag (release.yml job verify-plugin-channel).",
  "version": "0.8.0",
  "artifacts": {
    "plugin": {
      "id": "quay",
      "bundle-type": "marketplace",
      "note": "Distributed via marketplace JSON files (.claude-plugin/marketplace.json + plugin/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json) checked into the repo and version-bumped with each release. Not a GitHub Release asset — consumers install it with `claude plugin marketplace add` + `claude plugin install quay@quay`."
    }
  },
  "capabilities": [
